cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this atlas, please cite it and the data sources it builds on. The code is MIT
  licensed. The anatomy terms, definitions, synonyms and stage table are ZFIN data under CC BY
  4.0, and the ZFA and ZFS ontology files are CC BY 3.0. See public/ATTRIBUTION.md and
  LICENSE-DATA. The author built this software over three days with AI coding agents (Claude
  Code) working under his direction and review; the geometry is schematic, most size values are
  flagged estimates, and no independent anatomist has reviewed it.
title: Zebrafish 3D Atlas
abstract: >-
  An interactive 3D atlas of zebrafish development from the 1-cell zygote to the adult fish.
  Every shape is a procedural, schematic model placed in a body frame; the atlas draws no
  imaging mesh. Anatomy terms, definitions, synonyms and stage times come from ZFIN and the
  Zebrafish Anatomy and Stage Ontologies.
type: software
